  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4a03c4df-16a8-52ec-b525-7633880ed14d" activityNameId="ffbb3397-4cb0-5f01-8600-40be8f908215" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Copper, from imported concentrates, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Copper, from imported concentrates, at refinery
The product "copper, from imported concentrates, at refinery" is a auxiliary module used uniquely in the consumption mix in order to separate concentrate production and their transportation from different countries and the pyrolytical winning in RER. It does not contain any copper bearing inputs.;
CAS number: 007440-50-8; 
UUID: e20a48a9-1aa7-33a9-9458-16426ca004f3
The module includes the pre-treatment of the ore, reduction and refining of copper cathodes in RER. It does NOT include the mining and beneficiation step.
Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.
Technology: The ore is pre-treated, reduced and refined according to the country specific mix of process alternatives: reverberatory furnace 6.2%; flash smelting furnaces 76%; other 17.8%. An overall abatement for sulphur dioxide of 95% was estimated.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 193000 tonnes in 1994 from this source
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e20a48a9-1aa7-33a9-9458-16426ca004f3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="948c6fdb-25b0-54ae-bf5c-e320176f724c" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">DE</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.</text>
